:"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"M_Jr18nhOCBq462yQw12JQ","review_id":"oCwBOrkpBMnDcQuxLMGmgQ","date":"2013-04-22T01:34:48","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9362391829490662,"text_excerpt":"I know this may be blasphemy for the hard core Nola snoball aficionados but to me they are pretty much all the same. (Woah! That's 2 big words in one sentence!) There's your basic cherry, bubble gum, wedding cake, etc. stable flavors of snowballs that taste the same no matter where you go. I'm sure some peeps get all worked up about ice to syrup ratio but other that that it's the same. The thing that makes a snoball stand stand apart would be the variety of flavors, other stuff they serve, and location. That's where Piety Street Sno-Balls helps distance themselves from others. They have a nice size variety of snoball and even make some homemade crazy syrups. They serve ice cream as well a..."},{"business_id":"M_Jr18nhOCBq462yQw12JQ","review_id":"PrALP_hfbUpnrv8_KrdIcw","date":"2015-06-20T23:22:06","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9282626509666443,"text_excerpt":"Bywater is a low key unique and interesting part of New Orleans I haven't ventured through much. I recently was driving around there and found piety street Sno balls. I got a small raspberry zinger sno ball (raspberry flavor, vanilla ice cream in middle, whip cream and coconut shavings). It was amazing! Also about 4 dollars and barely a wait on a Saturday afternoon. Better than overrated Hansens Sno balls."},{"business_id":"M_Jr18nhOCBq462yQw12JQ","review_id":"W8yN9B0tBqaFZf-lEgvqTA","date":"2015-08-23T20:32:51","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9177996516227722,"text_excerpt":"I think Piety is tied with Hansens's for number one snoballs in the city for me. Super cute area. I think there might be a slight charge if you use card. So many flavored to choose from. Make half a day out of it: some lunch at Pizza D, walk across the street to grab some dessert at Piety, and take a walk through crescent city park to enjoy your snoball overlooking the river on a nice day."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
